-- NEGATIVE fixture, and AN UNPAID OBLIGATION rather than merely a fixture
-- (spec §6.4.5: "re-measure p5 after Phase 3").
--
-- p5: the cycle runs through a RECORD COMPUTED FIELD.
--
--     DECLARE Assessment
--       HAS `declared`  IS A NUMBER
--           `grossed`   IS A NUMBER  MEANS `the assessed total` PLUS `declared`
--     `the assessed total` MEANS `the case file`'s `grossed`
--
-- On the tree as of Phase 3, only ONE of the two edges emitted: `freeRefs`
-- filters projection FIELD names (Lower.hs:4469-4471), so the read of `grossed`
-- out of the record does not produce an edge back to whatever computes it, and
-- the DRG is acyclic even though the definitions are not.
--
-- WHY THE OBLIGATION IS NOW DUE. §6.4.5's instruction was to re-measure this
-- after Phase 3. Phase 3 landed 2026-07-29, AND Phase 3.6's hydration actively
-- rewires `dcnRequirements` around computed fields (§4.4.4, R11): a hydrated
-- record's computed field becomes a context ENTRY, and the enclosing decision
-- acquires the entry's dependencies. That is precisely the mechanism that could
-- turn the missing edge into a present one. Phase 5 inherits the instruction;
-- whoever wires this fixture must RE-MEASURE rather than copy this paragraph.
--
-- Expected: UNKNOWN, on purpose. Record the measurement here when it is taken,
-- with the date and the tree state, and say which of the two edges emitted.
--
--
-- PROVENANCE OF THIS HEADER. The .l4 source was typechecked (`l4 check`, clean)
-- when it was written on 2026-07-31, with a prebuilt CLI. The statements above
-- about what TODAY'S EXPORTER emits and reports are taken from spec
-- §6.4.2/§6.4.5's table and were NOT re-measured here: that session had no
-- build. Whoever wires these fixtures into jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs must MEASURE
-- the expectation rather than transcribe it.
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`.

IMPORT prelude

§ `cycle through a computed field`

DECLARE Assessment
  HAS `declared`  IS A NUMBER
      `grossed`   IS A NUMBER
        MEANS `the assessed total` PLUS `declared`

ASSUME `the case file` IS AN Assessment

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assessed total` MEANS
    `the case file`'s `grossed`
